# What the package ships of the desktop's installables (Gitea #271, ADR 0047).
#
# One path a line, under programs/desktop. Everything listed here ships,
# and so does every part it brings -- the `# part:` lines in its header,
# and a theme's `image` -- because a part goes where its owner goes. A part
# is never listed itself. The platform (wm/, widgets/, lib/, login/ and
# every file that says `# platform:` of itself) always ships and is not
# listed either. Anything else in the nine kind folders comes from the
# catalogue only.
#
# tools/ships.hibr reads this; the Makefile, tests/scopes.py,
# tools/docshots.py and tests/541-bare-desktop.t all ask it rather than
# keeping a rule of their own.

# The desktop's own apps, on the hibr menu. Their panes are their parts.
system/about.hibr
system/catalogue.hibr
system/clipboard.hibr
system/modman.hibr
system/notifications.hibr
system/screenshot.hibr
system/tasks.hibr

# The applications that ship, the owner's choice of 2026-10-17. Files,
# Terminal and Stickies bring their panes.
apps/files.hibr
apps/term.hibr
apps/Accessories/stickies.hibr
apps/Accessories/calc.hibr
apps/Accessories/clock.hibr
apps/Accessories/puzzle.hibr
apps/Accessories/imgview.hibr

# The desktop's own Control Panel panes, and the two dialogs that two of
# them open.
control-panel/aboutme.hibr
control-panel/appearance.hibr
control-panel/control-strip.hibr
control-panel/datetime.hibr
control-panel/desktop.hibr
control-panel/displays.hibr
control-panel/filetypes.hibr
control-panel/keyboard.hibr
control-panel/language.hibr
control-panel/mouse.hibr
control-panel/network.hibr
control-panel/networks.hibr
control-panel/pictures.hibr
control-panel/screensaver.hibr
control-panel/screenshots.hibr
control-panel/shortcuts.hibr
control-panel/sound.hibr
control-panel/versions.hibr
control-panel/wallpaper.hibr
control-panel/wallset.hibr
control-panel/windows.hibr

# The Control Strip's modules that belong to no app.
control-strip/cursor.hibr
control-strip/shadow.hibr
control-strip/theme.hibr
control-strip/wallpaper.hibr

# One screen saver, the owner's choice of 2026-10-17; the rest are in the
# catalogue. A saved choice that is not installed falls back to a random
# one of those that are.
savers/mystify.hibr

# The theme and colour schemes a desktop starts with: Classic, Midnight,
# and Paper, the one light scheme. The rest are in the catalogue.
themes/classic.json
colours/midnight.json
colours/paper.json

# No language beyond English, which needs no file: Arabic is in the
# catalogue, and a desktop set to a language it does not have says so in
# its log and draws in English. The pseudo-languages xx and xy are for
# checking this tree's layouts, and the suites read them from the tree.
